ents":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:00:08-07:00","id":462989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/453970-fun-with-bane-ideas?p=462877#post462877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was asking more if that was a good bane or not. Pulled that strait from old vampire-hunting stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry. I like the drawing on the folklore. While I like the effect, I'm wondering about it in play. If they drink, then they burn off the blood, do they still look bloated? There are different ways to look at it, I suppose -- when blood pool is full (or above half maybe), the effect occurs. Or maybe a combination of the two if you want to get more complex, with a Kindred who just topped off the tank looking swollen and bloated for several hours until the blood fully settles into the system. <br /> <br /> I just can't see a hungry vamp looking bloated after drinking a dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T20:22:09-07:00","id":463041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/453970-fun-with-bane-ideas?p=462989#post462989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, sorry. I like the drawing on the folklore. While I like the effect, I'm wondering about it in play. If they drink, then they burn off the blood, do they still look bloated? There are different ways to look at it, I suppose -- when blood pool is full (or above half maybe), the effect occurs. Or maybe a combination of the two if you want to get more complex, with a Kindred who just topped off the tank looking swollen and bloated for several hours until the blood fully settles into the system.<br /> <br /> I just can't see a hungry vamp looking bloated after drinking a dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Updated. Hope it works better for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T05:59:54-07:00","id":463378,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm mistaken, Vampires and Werewolves are mythologically related, so why not a bane that plays with that? The only ones I can think of right now though would be either a psychological NEED to hunt or being affected by the moon in some way.Maybe a penalty when unable to see the moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:15:44-07:00","id":463484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/453970-fun-with-bane-ideas?p=463378#post463378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm mistaken, Vampires and Werewolves are mythologically related, so why not a bane that plays with that? The only ones I can think of right now though would be either a psychological NEED to hunt or being affected by the moon in some way.Maybe a penalty when unable to see the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Moon Madness</b><br /> While the vampire is directly exposed to moonlight all her rolls to resist Frenzy are capped by her Humanity. If it is the full moon this changes to Humanity -2.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of the Predator</b><br /> Once every week the vampire must engage in a proper, visceral hunt. He must use physical actions, physical Disciplines and Lashing Out with the Monstrous Beast to hunt down his prey and must feed through an Assault. He may not use Social actions or Disciplines that may make the target a willing vessel. If he fails to engage in this behaviour all his dice pools are capped by his Humanity until he next indulges this strange need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:20:11-07:00","id":463607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/453970-fun-with-bane-ideas?p=463484#post463484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Moon Madness</b><br /> While the vampire is directly exposed to moonlight all her rolls to resist Frenzy are capped by her Humanity. If it is the full moon this changes to Humanity -2.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of the Predator</b><br /> Once every week the vampire must engage in a proper, visceral hunt. He must use physical actions, physical Disciplines and Lashing Out with the Monstrous Beast to hunt down his prey and must feed through an Assault. He may not use Social actions or Disciplines that may make the target a willing vessel. If he fails to engage in this behaviour all his dice pools are capped by his Humanity until he next indulges this strange need.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow, I really like these, partially because they are the sort of banes you'd want to keep hidden. I'll probably use one of these if I ever get to play in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:16:34-07:00","id":465668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/453970-fun-with-bane-ideas?p=461126#post461126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder if quicken sight would aid in counting lots of small things quickly, Ala Dracula 2 (The sequel to Dracula 2000).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:25:09-07:00","id":465674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/453970-fun-with-bane-ideas?p=463484#post463484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Moon Madness</b><br /> While the vampire is directly exposed to moonlight all her rolls to resist Frenzy are capped by her Humanity. If it is the full moon this changes to Humanity -2.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of the Predator</b><br /> Once every week the vampire must engage in a proper, visceral hunt. He must use physical actions, physical Disciplines and Lashing Out with the Monstrous Beast to hunt down his prey and must feed through an Assault. He may not use Social actions or Disciplines that may make the target a willing vessel. If he fails to engage in this behaviour all his dice pools are capped by his Humanity until he next indulges this strange need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are very good!<br /> <br /> Speaking of that--<br /> <br /> <b>Withering Hunger</b><b>: </b>Your character physically ages and withers when deprived of blood. Their hair turns white, their skin grows wrinkled and drawn, and their flesh and muscles shrivel under the burden of a strange accelerated age. When she has less than (10-Humanity) Vitae all her physical actions become capped by her humanity. Furthermore, all social interactions suffer a -1 penalty for every night she goes without mitigating the effect by feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T23:14:34-07:00","id":467035,"title":"","content":"Another--<br /> <br /> <b>Liturgy: </b>Your character finds that liturgies, last rites, and other spiritual observances for laying the dead to rest have the power to bring him closer to death as well. If such rites are performed in his presence while he is awake, bashing damage starts to accumulate for him every (Humanity) rounds he does not either flee from or stop the rites. If performed over him while in the daysleep, a Humanity roll must be made, with a failure resulting in him falling into torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}